cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software and research compendium, please cite this repository and the accompanying scientific article."
title: "Data and software for estimating electron density enhancements caused by solar flares using VLF time series"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Velásquez Ormaeche"
    given-names: "Juan Pablo"
    affiliation: "Comisión Nacional de Investigación y Desarrollo Aeroespacial (CONIDA)"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jpvelasquez/solar-flare-vlf-inversion"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
keywords:
  - VLF
  - ionospheric D region
  - solar flares
  - electron density
  - inverse problems
  - LongwaveModePropagator
  - Wait-Spies
  - SAVNET
  - reproducible research
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility package containing the code, curated notebooks,
  observational and synthetic data products, inversion outputs, and
  provenance records used to reconstruct solar-flare-driven D-region
  electron-density enhancements from VLF amplitude and phase time series
  on the NAA-PLO propagation path for the 25 March 2008 event.
